WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:06.714
From first kisses to YouTube makeup tutorials,
Wednesday Addams is in many ways your average American teen.

00:00:06.714 --> 00:00:09.581
But she hasn't let go of her ghoulish side
either.

00:00:09.905 --> 00:00:14.460
Most people think Wednesday Addams was born
on screen, but her debut came long before

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:16.690
the '60s sitcom The Addams Family.

00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:20.710
Like many popular characters, she got her
start in a comic strip penned by American

00:00:20.710 --> 00:00:22.740
cartoonist Charles Addams.

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:26.840
His woeful tales first appeared in the New
Yorker in 1938.

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:29.910
Addams also created work that wasn't all doom
and gloom.

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:33.820
But like Edgar Allan Poe, that's all that
people seem to remember him for.

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:37.960
Naming his creepiest characters after himself
certainly didn't help matters.

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:42.690
It also didn't help that, according to NPR,
his idea of a good time consisted of telling

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:47.600
his friends he visited insane asylums for
fun and offered to drive friends home — only

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:50.773
to seek out routes that passed dozens of cemeteries.

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:55.450
Wednesday Addams may have existed long before
she appeared on TV, but when she meandered

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:59.760
on her comic strip with the rest of her family,
she was actually nameless.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:03.760
According to a letter to the editor posted
in the New Yorker, Joan Blake, a mother in

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:07.820
a custody dispute, gave Addams inspiration
for Wednesday's name.

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:12.060
When Addams voiced his concern about not having
a name for the comic strip daughter as he

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:17.530
went into a TV show deal, Blake recited the
line of an old nursery rhyme, "Wednesday — Wednesday's

00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:18.990
child is full of woe."

00:01:18.990 --> 00:01:23.540
The cutesy rhyme is a fun adage meant to determine
what a child will be like depending on the

00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:25.060
day of the week they're born.

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:29.770
Funnily enough, Wednesday's middle name is
Friday in the sitcom, but despite her morbid

00:01:29.770 --> 00:01:34.506
tendencies, she's still pretty "loving and
giving," so it still tracks.

00:01:34.836 --> 00:01:39.220
It's pretty tricky to make a six-year-old
seem intimidating without going the full-on

00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:43.580
demonic route, and the '60s Addams Family
sitcom faced that very issue.

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:48.939
Sure, a young Lisa Loring was quite capable
of a fearless glower, but it usually prompted

00:01:48.939 --> 00:01:51.460
an "awws" rather than gasps.

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:56.219
Even her darkest lines don't seem so menacing
out of the mouth of the adorably braided child.

00:01:57.243 --> 00:01:58.077
"Nice knife.

00:01:58.077 --> 00:02:01.329
Can I play autopsy with it?"

00:02:01.329 --> 00:02:06.070
As a whole, Loring's Wednesday is kindhearted
and quick to help her family with any task

00:02:06.070 --> 00:02:09.778
that needs doing, even something as mundane
as fetching the mail.

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:16.449
"Thank you, Thing."

00:02:17.287 --> 00:02:23.019
But while the '60s series slightly muted her
angsty personality from the comics, the '90s

00:02:23.019 --> 00:02:27.430
films starring Christina Ricci brought her
back to her darker persona and aged her up

00:02:27.430 --> 00:02:30.690
a bit from the six-year-old she was at the
beginning of the show.

00:02:30.690 --> 00:02:34.959
From then on, she and Pugsley have flip-flopped
between being the older sibling in multiple

00:02:34.959 --> 00:02:37.550
projects the fictional Addams family starred
in.

00:02:37.861 --> 00:02:42.270
Everyone wants a piece of Wednesday Addams'
dishonor, including none other than the super

00:02:42.270 --> 00:02:44.440
sleuth pup, Scooby-Doo.

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:49.260
Wednesday appears in the episode "Wednesday
is Missing" of the confusingly titled TV series

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:50.940
The New Scooby-Doo Movies.

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:56.790
The episode, only the third in the series,
serves as the backdoor pilot to the 1973 animated

00:02:56.790 --> 00:02:58.360
Addams Family series.

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:03.239
When Morticia and Gomez Addams are looking
for some "us" time, the Scooby gang are hoodwinked

00:03:03.239 --> 00:03:07.310
into playing housekeepers for the wayward
Addams children after The Mystery Machine

00:03:07.310 --> 00:03:08.630
goes missing.

00:03:08.630 --> 00:03:13.030
Wednesday uncharacteristically wears a pink
version of her usual collared dress.

00:03:13.030 --> 00:03:17.659
However, she's still quick to get a "voodoo
booboo" while she sticks needles in a voodoo

00:03:17.659 --> 00:03:22.769
doll, so she definitely hasn't lost her spooky
streak beneath the smiles and the pink.

00:03:22.769 --> 00:03:27.069
Even her parents are disappointed with her
peppy demeanor, forlornly remarking that she's

00:03:27.069 --> 00:03:30.110
growing up to be a "sweet, cheerful young
lady."

00:03:30.110 --> 00:03:31.110
The horrors.

00:03:31.477 --> 00:03:36.319
One of the most hotly debated aspects of child
stars is kissing scenes that happen too soon

00:03:36.319 --> 00:03:37.569
for young actors.

00:03:37.569 --> 00:03:42.340
Whether it's in modern films and TV shows
or those of decades past, the concept of children

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:45.290
kissing will always garner a spirited discussion.

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:46.560
Where should we draw the line?

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:52.020
At just 13 years old, Ricci had her first
onscreen kiss with future Numb3rs star David

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:54.549
Krumholtz, who was only two years older.

00:03:54.549 --> 00:03:59.090
The Addams Family Values scene marked the
latter actor's first onscreen kiss as well.

00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:04.239
In a 1993 interview, Ricci was asked if there
was "a big to-do" made about the kiss.

00:04:04.239 --> 00:04:05.486
She brushed it off, saying,

00:04:13.989 --> 00:04:14.989
"The way memory works in childhood, it all
blurs.

00:04:14.989 --> 00:04:15.989
So I don't have a sense of who I was or what
I felt like before I was an actress, essentially."

00:04:15.989 --> 00:04:18.910
In a way, it's a little sad that Ricci had
to grow up quite so fast and in the limelight.

00:04:18.910 --> 00:04:23.110
While she may have told the interviewer that
it was no big deal, Krumholtz told Buzzfeed

00:04:23.110 --> 00:04:27.470
for the film's 20th anniversary that Ricci
was less than thrilled with her scene partner's

00:04:27.470 --> 00:04:28.247
peach fuzz.

00:04:28.247 --> 00:04:28.949
He noted,

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:35.530
Most child stars have done anything humanly
possible to distance themselves from their

00:04:35.530 --> 00:04:39.080
most iconic role, but Christina Ricci has
other ideas.

00:04:39.080 --> 00:04:44.120
She told the AV Club that the Addams Family
films have had "the biggest impact" on her

00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:45.410
"career and life."

00:04:45.410 --> 00:04:49.860
She remains fully aware of the role that defined
her career, and still feels a kinship toward

00:04:49.860 --> 00:04:51.363
her darker alter ego.

00:04:51.363 --> 00:04:55.249
"I just got to do a lot of weird things that,
you know, normally I wouldn't get to do."

00:04:55.249 --> 00:04:56.611
Ricci told the A.V. Club,

00:04:59.720 --> 00:05:04.310
We'll probably never know just how much the
role shaped Ricci as a person, but she's certainly

00:05:04.310 --> 00:05:08.880
defied the tragic fate of many child stars
– so maybe Wednesday's resilience and strength

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:14.150
played a part in Ricci's transition from a
child star to a successful adult actress.

00:05:14.150 --> 00:05:15.980
She posed this question to the AV Club:

00:05:23.169 --> 00:05:25.650
In a sobering follow-up thought, Ricci noted,

00:05:33.449 --> 00:05:38.486
So in a way, she and Wednesday are permanently
intertwined — for better or for worse.

00:05:38.970 --> 00:05:43.250
If you thought young Wednesday Addams is a
mood, she has nothing on comedian Melissa

00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:45.940
Hunter's Adult Wednesday Addams miniseries.

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:50.630
We first got a glimpse at Wednesday's enlightened
social views in Addams Family Values when

00:05:50.630 --> 00:05:55.260
she ranted during her camp's Thanksgiving
skit, which glorified the "peace" the pilgrims

00:05:55.260 --> 00:05:57.259
extended to the Native Americans.

00:05:57.259 --> 00:06:01.800
Hunter took the social commentary 10 steps
further with her ultra-feminist rendition

00:06:01.800 --> 00:06:07.730
of adult Wednesday as she tried to reconcile
her gloomy yet woke disposition amid the superficiality

00:06:07.730 --> 00:06:09.349
she faced in LA.

00:06:09.349 --> 00:06:13.940
Between savagely getting even with a handful
of cat-callers and showing an entitled "It

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:17.740
girl" who's boss, the show's 13 episodes weren't
nearly enough.

00:06:17.740 --> 00:06:22.410
"You want a book deal, but you can't afford
a ghostwriter so now you just post duck-faced

00:06:22.410 --> 00:06:25.205
selfies with your green juice every morning."

00:06:25.205 --> 00:06:30.419
Sadly, according to the Daily Dot, the Tee
&amp; Charles Addams Foundation wasn't as charmed

00:06:30.419 --> 00:06:34.900
as the show's millions of viewers, slapping
a lawsuit on the young comedian and her low-budget

00:06:34.900 --> 00:06:36.330
passion project.

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:41.259
After a copyright cease-and-desist forced
Hunter to take the series down in 2015, rumors

00:06:41.259 --> 00:06:46.169
floated around that the foundation took action
due to a planned MGM animated movie.

00:06:46.169 --> 00:06:50.479
It took years for the film to happen, but
that very well could have been why the foundation

00:06:50.479 --> 00:06:53.470
robbed us of a dry, witty, and woke Wednesday
Addams.

00:06:54.079 --> 00:06:59.481
Let's face it: We all have those days where
we feel like channeling our inner angsty Wednesday Addams.

00:06:59.481 --> 00:07:04.289
Luckily for those looking to get her pallid
complexion just right, MGM released a YouTube

00:07:04.289 --> 00:07:07.289
video called "Wednesday's Late-Nite Makeup
Tutorial."

00:07:07.289 --> 00:07:11.759
The video is perfect for anyone whose real-life
eye shadows aren't quite dark enough.

00:07:11.759 --> 00:07:13.919
And don't worry, as Wednesday notes in the
video:

00:07:13.919 --> 00:07:17.810
"Guaranteed to make you look like you
haven't slept in years."

00:07:17.810 --> 00:07:23.039
The video served to promote the release of
the 2019 animated film The Addams Family.

00:07:23.039 --> 00:07:27.700
Wednesday takes viewers through her arsenal
of makeup by brands like "Coverghoul's Depressed

00:07:27.700 --> 00:07:32.860
Powder," "Dry N Somber lip chalk," and the
very exclusive ashes of her ancestors.

00:07:32.860 --> 00:07:37.569
MGM also produced a video on "How To Make
Wednesday's Halloween Lemonade," and she wasn't

00:07:37.569 --> 00:07:40.610
the only Addams character to get some animated
YouTube love.

00:07:40.610 --> 00:07:46.099
There were even some Morticia, Gomez, and
Grandma tutorials to make your Halloween — or

00:07:46.099 --> 00:07:48.892
a random Wednesday afternoon — extra spooky.

00:07:49.334 --> 00:07:54.180
A Tim Burton-led Addams Family project has
been a long time coming — since the '90s,

00:07:54.180 --> 00:07:55.280
to be exact.

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:59.650
People usually assume that the macabre director
has helmed at least one of the "Addams Family"

00:07:59.650 --> 00:08:03.919
iterations that have graced the screen in
the past few decades, but sadly, that's not

00:08:03.919 --> 00:08:04.949
the case.

00:08:04.949 --> 00:08:09.660
According to Film Stories, Burton even turned
down the offer to direct the 1991 film, with

00:08:09.660 --> 00:08:12.740
the honor eventually going to Barry Sonnenfeld.

00:08:12.740 --> 00:08:17.620
Even the 2019 animated film seemed like a
Burton project, though Greg Tiernan and Conrad

00:08:17.620 --> 00:08:19.250
Vernon directed the film.

00:08:19.250 --> 00:08:24.349
As it turns out, the third time's the charm,
and Burton is finally lending his dismal expertise

00:08:24.349 --> 00:08:28.960
to the dastardly family in a live-action Netflix
series simply titled Wednesday.

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:33.570
The series, of course, focuses on everyone's
favorite angst queen: Wednesday Addams.

00:08:33.570 --> 00:08:38.307
But unlike her previous onscreen appearances,
the Addams' daughter will be aged up quite a bit.

00:08:38.307 --> 00:08:43.310
According to early reports, Wednesday's storyline
has a bit of a Nancy Drew vibe while she tries

00:08:43.310 --> 00:08:46.649
to solve a supernatural case from her parents'
past.

00:08:46.649 --> 00:08:50.856
With a slight nod to Edgar Allan Poe, she
attends Nevermore Academy.

00:08:51.161 --> 00:08:56.019
Jenna Ortega is already a Scream queen, but
playing Wednesday still proved a challenge.

00:08:56.019 --> 00:09:00.319
What typically makes Wednesday a fascinating
and status quo-defying child is just that

00:09:00.319 --> 00:09:01.779
— she's a child.

00:09:01.779 --> 00:09:06.290
Most people expect young girls to be docile,
frilly, and innocent when they've barely reached

00:09:06.290 --> 00:09:07.510
double digits.

00:09:07.510 --> 00:09:12.470
That stereotype has faced increasingly widespread
challenges in recent years, but it still hasn't

00:09:12.470 --> 00:09:16.950
fully gone away, and that's precisely what
makes Wednesday a fascinating character.

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:21.970
So, with an aged-up Wednesday, how did Ortega
and the Wednesday writers avoid making her

00:09:21.970 --> 00:09:24.130
a run-of-the-mill snarky teen?

00:09:24.130 --> 00:09:28.079
According to a conversation Ortega had with
EW, that was one of the biggest challenges

00:09:28.079 --> 00:09:29.302
of taking on the role.

00:09:29.302 --> 00:09:30.787
Ortega explained to the outlet:

00:09:46.060 --> 00:09:50.950
It's tough to film such a long series about
a sardonic and somewhat unemotional character,

00:09:50.950 --> 00:09:52.980
but Tim Burton knows what he's doing.

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:55.990
Ortega praised Burton's attention to detail
to EW, saying,

00:10:05.616 --> 00:10:09.700
Though Ortega noted some of the challenges
she had getting into character and keeping

00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:14.260
Wednesday fresh, Christina Ricci isn't worried
about the younger star's performance.

00:10:14.260 --> 00:10:19.408
As it turns out, Addams Family Values won't
be the last time fans see Ricci in this kooky world.

00:10:19.408 --> 00:10:24.089
Her role in Wednesday has given her a front-row
seat for Ortega's performance, and according

00:10:24.089 --> 00:10:26.519
to Ricci, she's living up to the hype.

00:10:26.519 --> 00:10:30.510
After applauding Tim Burton and Gwendolyn
Christie's work on the show during a Variety

00:10:30.510 --> 00:10:34.630
interview, Ricci deemed Ortega's performance
as Wednesday "incredible."

00:10:34.630 --> 00:10:35.630
Ricci told the outlet:

00:10:49.649 --> 00:10:53.670
If Ricci is down with Ortega's take on the
character, fans have gotten all the approval

00:10:53.670 --> 00:10:57.408
they need directly from a generation's favorite
onscreen Wednesday.

